// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§2.3", "§18.1"]

// (S-89, R-101.) E0001: a name is ASCII letters, digits and `_` (§2.3). Any other character in a name
// is E0001 (the message names the characters a name may use, which the markers do not compare),
// wherever a name is written: a binding, a function, a parameter, a field, a type, a constant, a
// flow, a pattern, a path, a name that only ends with such a character. Letters of other scripts
// and look-alikes (the Cyrillic `а`, U+0430) are no names, because the case of a letter decides the
// kind of a name and a look-alike cannot be told from the ASCII letter. One error per function
// (P-01); the same inputs inside comments and strings are fine (lex/ident_ascii_ok.onsa).

